---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Real Estate & Land Law" description="Land certificates, customary tenure, acquisition due diligence, leases, mortgages and land disputes in Cameroon.">
<div>
  <section style="max-width:1360px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(48px,7vw,104px) clamp(20px,5vw,80px) clamp(36px,4vw,56px)">
    <a href="/practices/" class="lnk" style="background:none;border:0;padding:0;cursor:pointer;font-size:12px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#007EA7;margin-bottom:26px">← Practices</a>
    <h1 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:300;font-size:clamp(36px,5.2vw,68px);line-height:1.06;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;max-width:20ch">Real Estate &amp; Land Law</h1>
    <p style="font-size:clamp(17px,1.4vw,20px);line-height:1.7;color:#38484f;max-width:66ch;margin:32px 0 0">Land in Cameroon is governed by the 1974 Land Ordinances and a registration system that sits alongside living customary tenure. Most disputes we see begin with a title that was never properly verified.</p>
  </section>
  <hr style="border:0;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14);margin:0" />
  <section style="max-width:1360px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5vw,80px)">
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(12,minmax(0,1fr));gap:32px">
      <aside style="grid-column:span 3;min-width:200px;align-self:start;position:sticky;top:110px;padding:clamp(32px,4vw,56px) 0">
        <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b7b82;margin-bottom:18px">On this page</div>
        <nav style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;border-left:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.16);padding-left:18px">
          <a href="#ordinances" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:#00171F">The 1974 Ordinances and registration</a>
          <a href="#national" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:#00171F">National lands and concessions</a>
          <a href="#customary" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:#00171F">Customary tenure and title</a>
          <a href="#dd" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:#00171F">Acquisition due diligence</a>
          <a href="#sequence" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:#00171F">Due-diligence sequence</a>
          <a href="#leases" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:#00171F">Leases and ground leases</a>
          <a href="#development" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:#00171F">Development and permitting</a>
          <a href="#mortgages" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:#00171F">Mortgages and land security</a>
          <a href="#expropriation" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:#00171F">Compulsory acquisition</a>
          <a href="#litigation" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:#00171F">Land disputes</a>
        </nav>
      </aside>
      <div style="grid-column:span 8;min-width:280px;padding:clamp(32px,4vw,56px) 0 clamp(48px,6vw,88px)">

        <section id="ordinances" style="scroll-margin-top:110px;padding-bottom:44px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14)">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 20px">The 1974 Land Ordinances and the land certificate</h2>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 16px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">The 1974 Ordinances reorganised land into national lands, state private and public property, and privately held registered land. The land certificate — the <em>titre foncier</em> — is the state’s official record of ownership and the starting point of any transaction.</p>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">We obtain certificates, act on transfers and mutations, and verify existing certificates at the land registry: chain of title, area and boundaries as surveyed, registered charges, and whether the certificate has been the subject of a challenge or a parallel grant.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="national" style="scroll-margin-top:110px;padding:44px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14)">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 20px">National lands, state property, grants and concessions</h2>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">Land held by the state is allocated by temporary grant, long lease or concession, each with development conditions and a route to definitive title once those conditions are met. We advise applicants on the consultative-board process, on the conditions attached to a grant, and on what happens when a development programme slips behind the timetable in the instrument.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="customary" style="scroll-margin-top:110px;padding:44px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14)">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 20px">Customary tenure and registered title</h2>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 16px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">In the Northwest and Southwest regions in particular, land is frequently occupied and transferred under customary arrangements that the register does not reflect. A valid certificate and a long-standing customary claim can point to the same parcel.</p>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">We investigate occupation on the ground, engage with families and traditional authorities, document consents and releases properly, and advise on how a court is likely to treat the competing positions. Buyers who skip this step usually pay for it later.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="dd" style="scroll-margin-top:110px;padding:44px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14)">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 20px">Acquisition due diligence, boundaries and competing claims</h2>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">Registry searches, instruction of a licensed surveyor, reconciliation of the survey plan with the certificate, physical inspection for occupation and encroachment, enquiry into pending proceedings, and structuring of the purchase so that price is released against registration rather than signature.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="sequence" style="scroll-margin-top:110px;padding:44px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14)">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 12px">Illustrative due-diligence sequence</h2>
          <p style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.65;color:#6b7b82;margin:0 0 28px;max-width:66ch">Diagram — a simplified, illustrative sequence for a registered-land acquisition. It is not legal advice, and the steps in any particular matter will differ.</p>
          <div style="display:grid;max-width:68ch;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.16)">
            <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:52px 1fr;gap:20px;padding:18px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.1)"><span style="font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13px;color:#007EA7">01</span><div><div style="font-size:16px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:4px">Identify the parcel</div><p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4a5a61">Certificate number, location, stated area, registered holder.</p></div></div>
            <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:52px 1fr;gap:20px;padding:18px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.1)"><span style="font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13px;color:#007EA7">02</span><div><div style="font-size:16px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:4px">Registry search</div><p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4a5a61">Chain of title, mutations, registered mortgages and restrictions.</p></div></div>
            <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:52px 1fr;gap:20px;padding:18px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.1)"><span style="font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13px;color:#007EA7">03</span><div><div style="font-size:16px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:4px">Survey and boundary check</div><p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4a5a61">Licensed surveyor reconciles the plan with the certificate and with what is on the ground.</p></div></div>
            <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:52px 1fr;gap:20px;padding:18px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.1)"><span style="font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13px;color:#007EA7">04</span><div><div style="font-size:16px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:4px">Occupation and customary enquiry</div><p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4a5a61">Site inspection; enquiry with neighbours, families and traditional authorities.</p></div></div>
            <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:52px 1fr;gap:20px;padding:18px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.1)"><span style="font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13px;color:#007EA7">05</span><div><div style="font-size:16px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:4px">Disputes and encumbrances</div><p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4a5a61">Pending proceedings, expropriation notices, planning constraints, unpaid land tax.</p></div></div>
            <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:52px 1fr;gap:20px;padding:18px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.1)"><span style="font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13px;color:#007EA7">06</span><div><div style="font-size:16px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:4px">Report and conditions</div><p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4a5a61">Findings, risks that can be cured before completion, and those that cannot.</p></div></div>
            <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:52px 1fr;gap:20px;padding:18px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.1)"><span style="font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13px;color:#007EA7">07</span><div><div style="font-size:16px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:4px">Deed and notarial steps</div><p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4a5a61">Execution, duties and fees, price released against registration milestones.</p></div></div>
            <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:52px 1fr;gap:20px;padding:18px 0"><span style="font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13px;color:#007EA7">08</span><div><div style="font-size:16px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:4px">Registration of the transfer</div><p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4a5a61">Mutation recorded; updated certificate obtained and checked.</p></div></div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="leases" style="scroll-margin-top:110px;padding:44px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14)">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 20px">Commercial and residential leases, ground leases</h2>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">Commercial leases under the Uniform Act on General Commercial Law, including renewal rights, rent review and the compensation payable on refusal to renew; residential tenancies; and long ground leases for industrial and retail development, where the interaction between the lease term and the tenant’s capital programme needs to be set out precisely.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="development" style="scroll-margin-top:110px;padding:44px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14)">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 20px">Development and construction; permitting</h2>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">Development agreements, construction contracts and consultant appointments, performance security and retention, building and subdivision permits, environmental and social requirements, and the sequencing of approvals against funding drawdowns.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="mortgages" style="scroll-margin-top:110px;padding:44px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14)">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 20px">Mortgages and land-based security</h2>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">Conventional and judicial mortgages over registered land, registration and ranking, security over leasehold interests and over land held under grant, releases on repayment, and enforcement by sale — including the practical obstacles enforcement meets where the land is occupied.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="expropriation" style="scroll-margin-top:110px;padding:44px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14)">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 20px">Compulsory acquisition and compensation</h2>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">Acting for owners, occupiers and businesses affected by acquisition for public purposes: participating in the enquiry and valuation process, challenging the assessment of crops, structures and business losses, and pursuing payment where an award has been made but not settled.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="litigation" style="scroll-margin-top:110px;padding:44px 0 0">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 20px">Land disputes and litigation strategy</h2>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 16px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">Competing certificates, boundary and encroachment claims, family and succession disputes over land, challenges to the issue of a certificate, and injunctions to stop works pending trial. We advise early on whether a case is better resolved by negotiated release and re-registration than by judgment.</p>
          <p style="font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:#6b7b82;margin:0;max-width:68ch">General information about the firm’s practice, not legal advice. No lawyer-client relationship arises from reading this page.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
</Base>
